10. Decision Protocol

10.1 Terminal states

State Condition Output
Construct \Delta_{\mathrm{HPTR}} > 0, non-reducible, coverage maintained HPTR v1.0 with demonstrated utility
Narrow \Delta_{\mathrm{HPTR}} > 0 on one metric only HPTR as single-purpose audit tool
Abandon \Delta_{\mathrm{HPTR}} \leq 0 Collision report as negative result
Change problem \Delta_{\mathrm{HPTR}} reveals a different, more tractable problem Redirected research program

10.2 Strict rules

\boxed{\Delta_{\mathrm{HPTR}} \leq 0 \Rightarrow \text{Abandon}}

\boxed{\Delta_{\mathrm{HPTR}} > 0 \ \land\ \text{non-reducible to } \mathcal{B}_1 \Rightarrow \text{Construct}}

Between the two, if the gain is real but limited:

\boxed{\text{Narrow}}

10.3 Prohibition on indefinite search

Indefinite search is avoidance. After the utility test, a terminal state must be declared. The collision report is itself a publishable output if the terminal state is Abandon or Narrow.

---

11. Conclusion

C1 is refined as conditional non-retroactivity: Y \to \mathcal{P}_t^{\text{past}} is not automatically invalid; only Y \to necessity of the realized past requires independent identification. C2 is a provenance triple, not a semiring. C3 is absorbed into C4. C4 is measure-transformation attribution. The categorical layer is conjectural and excluded from the benchmark.

HPTR v1.0 status.

\boxed{\text{Conceptual framework} = \text{frozen}}

\boxed{\text{Novelty} = \text{no single element novel; joint audit capacity undemonstrated}}

\boxed{\text{Utility} = \text{falsifiable by the specified benchmark}}

\boxed{\text{Primary question} = \text{can } \mathcal{B}_2 \text{ reduce false attribution without sacrificing coverage?}}

\boxed{\text{Decision variable} = \Delta_{\mathrm{HPTR}} = \mathcal{B}_2 - \mathcal{B}_1}

\boxed{\text{Decision} = \text{Construct if } \Delta_{\mathrm{HPTR}} > 0 \text{ and non-reducible; Abandon if } \Delta_{\mathrm{HPTR}} \leq 0}

Guiding principle. We no longer argue about novelty. We put HPTR in competition with what exists. If \Delta_{\mathrm{HPTR}} \leq 0, the architecture adds no demonstrated value and is abandoned without regret. If \Delta_{\mathrm{HPTR}} > 0 and non-reducible, we have something more interesting than a novelty claim: a demonstrable methodological advantage.

No claim of utility is admitted until \Delta_{\mathrm{HPTR}} is measured. No algebraic claim is admitted without the corresponding proposition being proven. No categorical claim is admitted without the corresponding functorial properties being verified.

