Appendix F — Benchmark Full Specification

F.1 Synthetic data-generating process

Input parameters.

Symbol Meaning Default
N Number of trajectories 1000
\|\mathcal{F}\| Size of transformation space 8
\rho Masking level 0.3
p_{\text{fam}} Family distribution Uniform over \{I, II, III, IV\}
p_{IV} Type IV sub-family distribution Uniform over \{a, b, c, d\}
\sigma_Y Observation noise 0.1
K Replications 10

Algorithm F.1 (Data generation).

```
For i = 1 to N:
    F_i^true ~ Uniform(F)

    τ_i ~ GenerateTrajectory(F_i^true)

    D_i^doc ~ GenerateDocuments(τ_i, ρ)

    family_i ~ Categorical(p_fam)

    If family_i ∈ {I, II, III}:
        O_i ~ IndependentlyJustifiedModel(D_i^doc)
    Else:
        O_i ~ SubFamilyModel(family_i, F_i^true, D_i^doc)

    Y_i ~ O_i(· | F_i^true)

    If family_i = IV:
        sub_fam_i ~ Categorical(p_IV)
        F_i^{true,twin} ~ ChooseTwin(F_i^true, sub_fam_i)
        τ_i^twin ~ GenerateTrajectory(F_i^{true,twin})
        D_i^{doc,twin} ~ GenerateDocuments(τ_i^twin, ρ)
            subject to observational equivalence with D_i^doc
        O_i^twin ~ MatchingObservationModel(O_i, D_i^{doc,twin})
        Y_i^twin ~ O_i^twin(· | F_i^{true,twin})
            subject to observational equivalence: Y_i^twin = Y_i

Return: {(D_i^doc, Y_i, O_i, F_i^true, family_i)}_{i=1}^N
```

Remark F.1. Twin generation enforces:

\forall g \text{ observationally measurable}: \quad g(D_i^{doc}, Y_i, O_i) = g(D_i^{doc,twin}, Y_i^{twin}, O_i^{twin}).

This is by construction: D_i^{doc,twin} has matching observables; Y_i^{twin} = Y_i; O_i^{twin} matches O_i on observables.

F.2 Case family generators

Family I (Identifiable). Trajectory observed at high resolution (low \rho); O_i independently justified; no selection bias. F_i^{\text{true}} is uniquely recoverable.

Family II (Partially identifiable). Trajectory observed at moderate resolution; multiple F values compatible with D_i^{doc}.

Family III (Non-identifiable). Trajectory observed at low resolution; many F values compatible.

Family IV (Retroactivity trap).

Sub-family Y \to \mathcal{P}_t^{\text{past}} Ground truth
IV.a Outcome-as-evidence Legitimate via O O independently justified
IV.b Outcome-as-causal-reconstruction Illegitimate Y used to infer past impossibility
IV.c Independent historical constraint Legitimate via source at t Not via Y
IV.d Selection/survivorship trap Illegitimate Y correlates with survival, not exclusion

F.3 Counterfactual twin construction

Algorithm F.2 (Twin construction for Type IV).

For each Type IV case (D_i^{doc}, Y_i, O_i, F_i^{true}):

1. Sample F_i^{true,twin} \in \mathcal{F} \setminus \{F_i^{true}\}.
2. Generate \tau_i^{twin} consistent with F_i^{true,twin}.
3. Generate D_i^{doc,twin} such that observables match D_i^{doc} exactly.
4. Set O_i^{twin} = O_i (as function on observables).
5. Set Y_i^{twin} = Y_i.

Twin discrimination test. A system with outputs \widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^\star_i and \widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^{\star,twin}_i is tested on:

\text{Twin discrimination}_i =
\begin{cases}
1 & \text{if } \widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^\star_i \neq \widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^{\star,twin}_i \\
0 & \text{if } \widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^\star_i = \widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^{\star,twin}_i
\end{cases}

Correct behavior: 0 (indistinguishable by observational equivalence).

F.4 Observation models

Independently justified O. Constructed from D_i^{doc} alone: O(y \mid \theta) is the likelihood of y given \theta under a model fit to D_i^{doc} without using Y.

Non-independently justified O. Constructed by fitting to Y: O is chosen to maximize fit to the observed Y. Used in IV.b and IV.d.

F.5 Selection/survivorship mechanism

For Type IV.d, introduce a survival variable S \in \{0, 1\} such that

P(S = 1 \mid F^{\text{true}} = \theta) = \sigma(\theta)

for a monotone \sigma. Y_i is observed only if S = 1. The observed Y_i is correlated with survival, not with F^{\text{true}} directly.

F.6 Implementation of \mathcal{B}_0, \mathcal{B}_1, \mathcal{B}_2

\mathcal{B}_0 (Partial identification).

\widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^\star_{\mathcal{B}_0, i} = \{\theta \in \mathcal{F} : \mathcal{R}_m(D_i^{doc}) \in \mathcal{I}^{-1}(\theta) \text{ and } \theta \text{ satisfies } H\} \cap \{\theta : Y_i \in \operatorname{supp}(O_i(\cdot \mid \theta))\}.

\mathcal{B}_1 (\mathcal{B}_0 + standard provenance). Augment \mathcal{B}_0 with a W3C PROV-O provenance graph:

· Each document in D_i^{doc} is an Entity.
· \mathcal{R}_m is an Activity.
· The attribution A_i is an Activity.
· Standard PROV relations are recorded.

Output: \widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^\star_{\mathcal{B}_1, i} = \widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^\star_{\mathcal{B}_0, i}.

\mathcal{B}_2 (\mathcal{B}_1 + hypothesis-assignment provenance + conditional non-retroactivity).

Step 1. Build \operatorname{Prov}(q) = (D_q, H_q, \Pi_q) for every query q.

Step 2. Apply conditional non-retroactivity:

· If the inference uses Y without an independently justified O:

\widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^\star_{\mathcal{B}_2, i} := \widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^\star_{\mathcal{B}_1, i} \cup \{\theta \in \mathcal{F} : Y_i \text{ compatible with } \theta \text{ under any } O\}.

· If the inference uses Y via an independently justified O:

\widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^\star_{\mathcal{B}_2, i} := \{\theta \in \mathcal{F} : Y_i \in \operatorname{supp}(O_i(\cdot \mid \theta))\} \cap \widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^\star_{\mathcal{B}_1, i}.

Step 3. Load-bearing hypothesis analysis:

H_i^{\text{load}} := \{h \in H_q : q \text{ changes materially under } h'\}.

Output: (\widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^\star_{\mathcal{B}_2, i}, H_i^{\text{load}}).

F.7 Metrics

For each i and each \mathcal{B} \in \{\mathcal{B}_0, \mathcal{B}_1, \mathcal{B}_2\}:

Metric Definition
\operatorname{Coverage}_i \mathbf{1}[F_i^{\text{true}} \in \widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^\star_{\mathcal{B}, i}]
\operatorname{Sharpness}_i 1 - \|\widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^\star_{\mathcal{B}, i}\| / \|\mathcal{F}\|
\operatorname{FAR}_i \mathbf{1}[\widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^\star_{\mathcal{B}, i} = \{\theta\} \text{ with } \theta \neq F_i^{\text{true}}]
Retroactivity detection For IV.b/IV.d: 1 if \mathcal{B}_2 flags the inference as unidentified; else 0
False retroactivity For IV.a/IV.c: 1 if \mathcal{B}_2 flags the inference as unidentified; else 0
Hypothesis diagnosis Jaccard similarity J_i between true and estimated load-bearing sets
Twin discrimination For IV: 1 if \widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^\star_{\mathcal{B}, i} \neq \widehat{\mathfrak{A}}^{\star,twin}_{\mathcal{B}, i}; else 0

Aggregate metrics.

\operatorname{Coverage}_{\mathcal{B}} = \frac{1}{N} \sum_i \operatorname{Coverage}_i, \quad
\operatorname{FAR}_{\mathcal{B}} = \frac{1}{N} \sum_i \operatorname{FAR}_i,

\operatorname{HD}_{\mathcal{B}} = \frac{1}{N} \sum_i J_i, \quad
\operatorname{TDR}_{\mathcal{B}} = \frac{1}{N_{IV}} \sum_{i \in IV} \text{Twin discrimination}_i.

F.8 Sample size and power

For a two-sided test at \alpha = 0.05 with power 1 - \beta = 0.8, detecting effect size \delta in FAR:

N \geq \frac{2 (z_{\alpha/2} + z_\beta)^2}{\delta^2}.

For \delta = 0.1, N \geq 2(1.96 + 0.84)^2 / 0.01 \approx 1572.

Default: N = 1000 with K = 10 replications for effective N_{\text{eff}} = 10{,}000.

F.9 Preregistered decision rule

Let

\Delta_{\mathrm{FAR}} := \operatorname{FAR}_{\mathcal{B}_1} - \operatorname{FAR}_{\mathcal{B}_2},

\Delta_{\mathrm{Cov}} := \operatorname{Coverage}_{\mathcal{B}_2} - \operatorname{Coverage}_{\mathcal{B}_1},

\Delta_{\mathrm{HD}} := \operatorname{HD}_{\mathcal{B}_2} - \operatorname{HD}_{\mathcal{B}_1},

\Delta_{\mathrm{TDR}} := \operatorname{TDR}_{\mathcal{B}_1} - \operatorname{TDR}_{\mathcal{B}_2}.

Primary outcome (Construct).

\Delta_{\mathrm{FAR}} > 0, \quad \Delta_{\mathrm{Cov}} \geq -\varepsilon \ (\varepsilon = 0.02), \quad \Delta_{\mathrm{HD}} > 0, \quad \Delta_{\mathrm{TDR}} > 0,

all significant at p < 0.05 after Bonferroni correction over four metrics.

Secondary outcome (Narrow). \Delta_{\mathrm{FAR}} > 0 and either \Delta_{\mathrm{HD}} \leq 0 or \Delta_{\mathrm{TDR}} \leq 0, significant at p < 0.05.

Null outcome (Abandon). \Delta_{\mathrm{FAR}} \leq 0 or \Delta_{\mathrm{Cov}} < -\varepsilon.

Indispensability of the twin test. For the primary outcome to count, \Delta_{\mathrm{TDR}} > 0 is required at p < 0.05.

